<title>UK: Salvesen in talks to sell U.S. storage unit.</title>
<headline>Salvesen in talks to sell U.S. storage unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christian Salvesen Plc, the British distribution and equipment hire group, said on Thursday it is in talks with a number of potential buyers over the sale of its U.S. refrigerated warehousing business, CS Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposed sale of our American refrigerated warehousing business is in line with our strategy of focusing resources on major growth areas in which we have a strong market position,&quot; said Chris Masters, chief executive of Christian Salvesen in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
